  const g = grounded ? groundedGuard(text, context) : text;
  if (!g) return new Response(JSON.stringify({ answer: '', source: 'fallback', detail: ['guard-emptied'] }), { headers });
  return new Response(JSON.stringify({ answer: g, source: 'gemini' }), { headers });

The groundedGuard call near line 262 (Ollama path) and local-llm-proxy.mjs line 106 need the same change. groundedHybrid already returns null on source 'fallback' (and on an empty answer), so the page then shows kbBody(hit, q) with no change to chatbot.html.

Optional second change: also split on a space or ๆ in the groundedGuard split, so a single bad clause does not take the whole answer. The split should be done carefully, because Thai words are not space-delimited and a space is only a clause break in practice.

Also add a unit test under tests/ or benchmark/ that checks a single-paragraph answer with an invented number yields source 'fallback'.
